---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/layout/PageHeader.astro';
import Prose from '../components/sections/Prose.astro';
import { legal, entityName, entityPlace } from '../lib/legal';
---

<Base
  title="Terms — MindStack"
  description="The terms that apply to using this website, and how they relate to client work."
  quiet
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Legal"
    title="Terms"
    lead="These terms cover the use of this website. They are not the agreement under which we do client work — that is always a separate, signed document."
  />

  <Prose updated={legal.updated}>
    <h2>What these terms cover</h2>
    <p>
      This website is published by {entityName}, based in {entityPlace}. By using it you accept the
      terms below. If you do not accept them, please do not use the site.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Nothing on this website is a contract, a quote, or a binding offer.</strong> Project
      work is governed by a separate agreement — a proposal, statement of work, or services contract
      signed by both sides. Where anything on this site conflicts with a signed agreement, the signed
      agreement wins.
    </p>

    <h2>Using the site</h2>
    <p>You may read, share and link to anything here. Please do not:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>attempt to gain unauthorised access to the site or the systems behind it</li>
      <li>interfere with its availability for other people</li>
      <li>submit anything unlawful, or use the contact form to send bulk or automated messages</li>
      <li>copy substantial parts of the site to present as your own work</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Our content</h2>
    <p>
      The text, design, layout, code and marks on this site belong to {entityName} unless stated
      otherwise. Client names, logos and interface screenshots belong to their respective owners and
      appear here with permission.
    </p>

    <h2>Accuracy and no warranty</h2>
    <p>
      We write this site in good faith and keep it current, but we provide it "as is" and without
      warranties of any kind. Descriptions of past projects describe what we built for a particular
      client under particular constraints. They are not a promise of the same outcome, cost or
      timeline for your situation.
    </p>
    <p>
      Technical opinions on this site are opinions. Please do not treat them as a substitute for
      advice on your own systems, which we would only give after actually looking at them.
    </p>

    <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
    <p>
      We link to client work and to third-party tools. We do not control those sites and are not
      responsible for their content, availability or privacy practices.
    </p>

    <h2>Availability</h2>
    <p>
      We aim to keep this site up, but we do not guarantee uninterrupted availability. We may change
      or remove any part of it, including published project descriptions, without notice.
    </p>

    <h2>Liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, {entityName} is not liable for any indirect or
      consequential loss arising from your use of this website, or from reliance on anything
      published on it. Nothing here limits liability that cannot be limited by law.
    </p>

    <h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of {legal.jurisdiction}, and the courts of{' '}
      {legal.jurisdiction} have jurisdiction over any dispute arising from them.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms; the date at the top shows when they last changed. Questions go to{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${legal.contactEmail}`}>{legal.contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</Base>
